  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Relief Items Supply Chain of Humanitarian Organizations through the Strategic Joint Approach of the Quality, Social, and Environmental (QSE) Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian supply chain community is currently confronted with challenges in terms of funding, environmental footprint, preparedness, localization and coordination. Organizations must collaborate further to avoid competing and increasing costs. At the same time, supply chains must become greener. 
 
The International Organization for Migration, on behalf of the Quality, Social, and Environmental (QSE) Procurement Sub-group, is managing this project to strengthen the cooperation of the humanitarian sector regarding the procurement of relief items. This project&#x2019;s objective is to make humanitarian supply chain more effective and efficient by improving the quality of the largest impact relief items, whilst also ensuring that environmental and social concerns are addressed in their manufacture.</narrative>
  </description>
